JOURNALCTL - query the session journal
Usage: journalctl [--unit=<name>] [--level=<lvl>] [--lines=<n>] [unit]

Reads the kernel journal the way journalctl reads the systemd one. With
no arguments it prints everything since boot.

--unit=<name>   only entries mentioning <name>
--level=<lvl>   minimum level: debug, info, warn, error
--lines=<n>     only the last n entries
[unit]          shorthand for --unit=<unit>

Examples:
  journalctl --unit=sshd
  journalctl --level=warn --lines=20
  journalctl cloverd
